  "step_3": "The relevant information for the decision reason is the probability mass on favorable outcomes: A has 50% (25% + 25%), B has 25%. This makes A more left-skewed according to the defined rule (greater probability on favorable outcomes). The individual, however, does not consider this probabilistic structure. Instead, the individual focuses on the number of outcomes and the count of positive scenarios (two vs one), which is a different reasoning path. The justification does not refer to the distribution of probabilities or skewness. Therefore, even though the decision (choosing A) aligns with the outcome of the reason (A is more left-skewed), the individual did not use the skewness-based rule in their justification. The reasoning is based on a different principle — number of positive outcomes — not on the probability distribution of favorable vs unfavorable outcomes. Hence, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process. The individual did not evaluate or mention skewness or the probability mass on favorable outcomes. Thus, the reason was not applied.",
